{#-
  The generated block in every role README.

  aar-doc loads its *content* template from inside its own package, which cannot
  be replaced. Its *output* template can be a file, and it receives the same
  data, so this file ignores `content` and renders the block itself.

  Two things it deliberately leaves out:

  * `galaxy_collection.version`. The stock template prints it, which would make
    every release rewrite every role README and turn the docs-current gate red
    on the Release PR.
  * A level-1 heading, a License section and an Author section. The README's
    prose owns those; this block owns the interface.

  The BEGIN/END markers must be emitted here: aar-doc replaces the marker lines
  themselves, not just what lies between them.
-#}
